{
  "about": "The Studio page registry, read by serve.py (the /hub/assets allowlist, the stylesheet links and an inline copy in the hub page, the reserved server paths) and by the hub through that copy (pages.js). A page entry: id, label, icon (icons.js name), nav (its place in the sidebar), renderer (builtin: a view in hub.js), js and css (its files under alpaca/web), endpoints (the server paths it reads; profile routes are not listed), needs (the live flags it reads, liveflags.js), quiet (a live refresh patches it in place), timer (the 15 s overview timer refreshes it), loader (its loading steps, loader.js; none means the record steps), gate (profile: shown only when the profile turns it on), profile_routes (the profile routes a gated page reads: it shows only when the profile serves every one), divider (a rule above it in the nav). A project adds pages of its own through its profile, not here (docs/studio.md 4.0). Stylesheets link in this order: shell css_before, then each page's css in the order of this list, then shell css_after.",
